# =============================================================================
# PLACEHOLDER / TEMPLATE — GitHub read token for the self-heal metrics exporter.
#
# This is a *.template file on purpose: it is NOT a real SealedSecret and is NOT
# synced by Argo (the fuzeinfra-sealed-secrets Application recurses
# deploy/sealed-secrets/ for *.yaml; a `.template` suffix is excluded). It exists
# so the credential-wiring path is committed and reviewable WITHOUT committing a
# real token. Seal the real file next to it as
# deploy/sealed-secrets/selfheal-metrics-github-token.yaml.
#
# ── This secret is OPTIONAL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Deployment references it with `optional: true`
# (helm/fuzeinfra/templates/selfheal-metrics.yaml). Without it the exporter runs
# unauthenticated against the public GitHub REST API — the counts are identical,
# the only difference is the rate limit: 60 requests/hour instead of 5000. At the
# default 10-minute poll over 3 labels that is ~18 req/h, so unauthenticated is
# genuinely workable. Seal a token when the label map grows or the repo goes
# private, not as a prerequisite for enabling the exporter.
#
# ── Keys this Secret must carry ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#   token   A GitHub token with READ-ONLY access to izzywdev/FuzeInfra issues.
#           A fine-grained PAT with `Issues: Read` (or `Contents: Read` on a
#           public repo) is sufficient — the exporter only ever issues
#           GET /repos/{repo}/issues. Give it NOTHING else: this pod's stdout is
#           shipped to Loki and its metrics are scraped by Prometheus, so the
#           blast radius of a leak is the token's own scope.
#
#           Alphanumeric-only is not achievable for a GitHub PAT (they contain
#           `_`), but it must have NO trailing newline — `printf %s`, never
#           `echo`, or the newline becomes part of the Authorization header and
#           every call 401s.
#
# ── How to produce the real file (human, one-time, offline) ──────────────────
#   printf %s '<GITHUB READ-ONLY PAT>' > /tmp/selfheal_token
#   scripts/seal-secret.sh fuzeinfra/selfheal-metrics-github-token \
#     token=@/tmp/selfheal_token \
#     --out deploy/sealed-secrets/selfheal-metrics-github-token.yaml
#   shred -u /tmp/selfheal_token
#
# Sealing needs no cluster access — see docs/SECRETS_MANAGEMENT.md §1 for the
# published public cert and the container fallback when kubeseal is unavailable.
#
# ── After a reseal ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kubernetes does not restart a pod when a Secret it reads as env changes, and
# Argo applies this ciphertext from OUTSIDE the Helm release, so the chart cannot
# hash it. Roll the pod by hand after a rotation:
#   kubectl -n fuzeinfra rollout restart deploy/fuzeinfra-selfheal-metrics
# There is no `secretRotation` knob here (unlike handoffMcp) because a stale
# token degrades to unauthenticated polling, not to a silent auth failure.
#
# ── Shape of the REAL sealed output (for reference only) ─────────────────────
# apiVersion: bitnami.com/v1alpha1
# kind: SealedSecret
# metadata:
#   name: selfheal-metrics-github-token
#   namespace: fuzeinfra
# spec:
#   encryptedData:
#     token: AgB...   # ciphertext, safe to commit
#   template:
#     metadata:
#       name: selfheal-metrics-github-token
#       namespace: fuzeinfra
#     type: Opaque
# =============================================================================
